## Tech Debt Audit

When asked to audit tech debt:

- Search all source files for TODO, FIXME, HACK, XXX markers; read 5 lines of context around each to assess severity.
- Check dependency files for stale packages (2+ major versions behind), deprecated packages, and packages with known CVEs.
- Scan for deprecated API usage: @Deprecated, deprecated(), DeprecationWarning, or framework-level deprecations.
- Identify untested critical paths: auth, payments, data migrations, and core business logic with no corresponding test coverage.
- Flag hardcoded config: IP addresses, hostnames, staging URLs, ports, credentials, or environment-specific values in source.
- Flag dead feature flags: flags always evaluated to the same value with no mechanism to change them.
- Estimate blast radius per item: High (critical flow, 5+ dependents), Medium (secondary flow, 2–4 dependents), Low (isolated).
- Order findings P0 (hardcoded credential, untested auth/payment, deprecated security API) through P3 (low-impact TODO, outdated but functioning dep) with file:line, blast radius, and a one-line remediation note each.
